{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05XX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$F : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\times \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0007": "$F$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-map-from-algebraic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:22a13cea5d4467f2095a9a1ddbff4fe10b272f06ddec3569ee52ae9b56cedba1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2e5b8a8caa2bfe8bbcd0d46bb965bf9621b9b6c6efe44ebb86560477ed9608d5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a <MATH_0003>-morphism\nof stacks in groupoids over <MATH_0004>. If <MATH_0005> is an\nalgebraic stack and <MATH_0006>\nis representable by algebraic spaces, then <MATH_0007> is algebraic.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ade282ac0e327927aec19a86d5d929ad49b9479158c60577452bf02826eb0c11", "unit_id": "tag:06CG:statement"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05XX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0002": "$1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0007": "$T$", "MATH_0008": "$2$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n(\\Sch/T)_{fppf} \\times_{\\xi, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{U}\n\\longrightarrow\n(\\Sch/T)_{fppf} \\times_{\\xi, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-representable-by-spaces}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-representable-transformations-property}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-representable-diagonal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-smooth-surjective-morphism-implies-algebraic}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b82ea2bc077152998c7f30a4a547b6ac5789afdc6a0561694f287079a7f723da", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1360c86e6b173ee82df5bcb1bb9f77436bc5bc3ad428abaa7b640bb939578f81", "source_text": "Choose a representable stack in groupoids <MATH_0001> and a surjective\nsmooth <MATH_0002>-morphism <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004> be a scheme and\nlet <MATH_0005> be an object of <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>. The morphism of\n<MATH_0008>-fibre products\n<MATH_0009>\nis representable by algebraic spaces, surjective, and smooth as a\nbase change of <MATH_0010>, see\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nBy our condition on the diagonal of <MATH_0011> we see that\nthe source of this morphism is representable by an algebraic space, see\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nHence the target is an algebraic stack by\nAlgebraic Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:000dbed108f525fa95210c90110abf03858520c